WEBVTT

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.370
It is the end of the 19th century.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:19.830
Amidst the turmoil and development
of the Industrial Revolution,

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.830
Britain steadily expands its colonization,

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.660
until its territories extend
to one quarter of the world,

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:29.120
becoming the empire on which the sun never sets.

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:31.540
This, the greatest empire in all of history,

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:38.410
is ruled by a privileged class that makes up
less than 3% of its population.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.830
In contrast with the advancement of technology,

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:44.450
an age-old class system remains
rooted throughout the land.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:48.410
This system, which divides people
amongst rigid boundaries,

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:52.620
and assigns the relative merits
of a life based on birth,

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.950
inevitably creates discrimination
between people.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.750
You seem to enjoy horse racing.

00:01:20.790 --> 00:01:25.580
You have been reading the racing
sheet quite intently, after all.

00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:29.290
Oh, how embarrassing.
I suppose I am more of a dabbler.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:32.250
My wife tells me that if I have
money to give to the horses,

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:36.660
I should replace the wallpaper first.

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:40.790
Well then, could I offer you some assistance?

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:42.620
I may be able to afford you the means

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:47.080
to acquire your new wallpaper, as well as
a bouquet of flowers for your wife.

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:50.750
You aren't saying you know
which horses will win, are you?

00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:57.620
Horse racing is a game that can usually be won
if one analyses the data at hand.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.000
<i>The mist is hiding the sin</i>

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:12.750
<i>I hold in my hand the LIST of judgment</i>

00:02:12.750 --> 00:02:15.370
<i>I'm gonna do the perfect crime</i>
<i>and bury them in a cist</i>

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:20.620
<i>That's my DYING WISH for you</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:26.040
<i>Guys of the privileged class torment the weak</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:29.120
<i>And they enjoy it</i>

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:34.660
<i>That's a bloody world, an endlessly</i>
<i>discriminatory society (dystopia)</i>

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:39.700
<i>Happiness does not bloom here</i>
<i>(Set a thief to catch another thief)</i>

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:42.830
<i>We are oppressed</i>

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:48.410
<i>We must do something. Come on</i>

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:54.870
<i>Let the end begin</i>

00:02:54.870 --> 00:03:00.700
<i>Break it to relieve your soul</i>

00:03:00.700 --> 00:03:06.620
<i>Open your eyes. You'll be reborn</i>
<i>when you lose your life</i>

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:11.700
<i>Lord of crime hora yume no ikenie</i>
<i>We're lords of crime. We're sacrifice for ideals</i>

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:24.000
<i>Freedom lives forever, even if we die</i>

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:38.830
"The Scarlet Eyes Act 1"

00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:38.830
What about the upcoming Wessex Cup?

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:40.330
Which horse should I bet on?

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:42.450
Why, the winning horse.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.500
Well, it wouldn't be sporting
if I knew which one it was.

00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:47.660
John Striker's horse.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:53.750
The horse belonging to John
Striker, the trainer, will win.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:59.870
Y-You're sure about that?

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.950
I cannot be certain,
but the odds are favourable.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:07.160
Come to think of it, the young master
predicted the last race, too.

00:04:07.160 --> 00:04:10.410
You can't, by any chance,
see into the future, can you?

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:14.120
Of course not. I just analysed the data.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:17.870
Horse racing is a game that you can win
about 80% of the time by doing so.

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:29.250
Analyse the data?
And you can tell from doing so?

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.660
Search me.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:37.200
Well, unlike us, folks in the upper class
have their fancy learning.

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.120
Young master!

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:41.870
Please, I need your wisdom.

00:04:41.870 --> 00:04:46.370
The flowers I sell wither up in no time
when I keep them at home.

00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:53.200
Put a little vinegar into the pail
in which you store your water.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:56.410
Vinegar? That's all I have to do?

00:04:56.410 --> 00:04:59.000
Yes. But only a little bit.

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:00.580
Young master!

00:05:00.580 --> 00:05:03.040
Thanks so much for your help!

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:08.000
I set out some strychnine
and the rats disappeared entirely.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.580
These are by way of thanks.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.040
They are?

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.870
Then I gladly accept.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:24.620
Brother...

00:05:24.620 --> 00:05:26.450
Out and about, I see.

00:05:26.450 --> 00:05:29.160
Yeah. I had some business to take care of.

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:31.580
Care to hop in? We can go home together.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:32.700
Right.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:36.500
Quite the smartly-dressed lad, but who is he?

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.000
Those are the Moriarty family's sons.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.370
Oh...

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:44.200
The oldest, Mr Albert,
and the second son, Master William.

00:05:44.200 --> 00:05:51.410
Hmm, but the young master there--
was that the way he looked?

00:05:59.290 --> 00:06:02.580
You seem to be as popular as ever.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:05.790
Did you get asked for your
advice about something again?

00:06:05.790 --> 00:06:09.700
Today it was flowers, and a little
nudging in a gambling matter.

00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:15.410
You're everyone's adviser,
or consultant, out here, too.

00:06:15.410 --> 00:06:20.000
That knowledge palace of yours
will be a world treasure someday.

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:22.910
You should keep on helping
people the way you are.

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:26.250
Yes, I am endeavouring to do so.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:29.950
Come to think of it,

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:34.410
I received these from a gentleman whom I advised
about a rat extermination matter the other day.

00:06:34.410 --> 00:06:37.910
Then those are your just desserts.

00:06:37.910 --> 00:06:42.450
I won't say anything to the others,
so you can eat them with Louis.

00:06:42.450 --> 00:06:44.580
Thank you very much.

00:06:44.580 --> 00:06:46.290
No...

00:06:46.290 --> 00:06:49.620
There will be hell to pay
if by some chance they find out...

00:06:51.450 --> 00:06:53.620
...so I'll be your partner in crime.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:03.910
Louis!

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:07.700
Welcome back, Brother.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:11.790
What are you doing? You should still be in bed.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:18.120
His limbs still work.
He can help out a little, can't he?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:23.120
But never mind him. On whose permission
did you ride in the family carriage?

00:07:23.120 --> 00:07:25.250
Mine.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.040
Mr Albert!

00:07:27.040 --> 00:07:27.700
--Welcome home, sir--

00:07:27.700 --> 00:07:30.040
--I let him ride in the carriage.
--Welcome home, sir--

00:07:30.040 --> 00:07:32.000
Is that good enough?

00:07:33.040 --> 00:07:36.040
I know that you are quite generous, Mr Albert,

00:07:36.040 --> 00:07:39.120
but you need to maintain an appropriate
distance from these two,

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.830
or I will receive a reprimand from her ladyship.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:44.540
Louis, take these.

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:45.790
Right.

00:07:45.790 --> 00:07:48.250
Take off that coat at once.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:56.540
Although they may be Mr Albert's hand-me-downs,
they are still too good for you.

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:02.870
You dare to clothe yourself in such
costly attire and stroll around town.

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:06.750
One could scarcely believe that not so long ago,

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:10.500
you were a child who was scrounging
for scraps of food in back alleys.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:16.250
Imagine, me ending up serving someone
of far lower class than myself.

00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:18.160
How low I have fallen.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:19.910
Simon!

00:08:19.910 --> 00:08:22.200
You speak too freely.

00:08:22.200 --> 00:08:23.580
--B-But, Mr Albert...

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:26.120
--What's all the commotion?
--B-But, Mr Albert...

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:31.790
I am ever so sorry...

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.750
...Master William.

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:58.040
You're going out, Brother?

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:02.700
Yes. Today is the day I go to the ragged school.

00:09:02.700 --> 00:09:05.160
You really are a curious one.

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:08.500
Even if you are doing this for
the Charity Organization Society,

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:13.500
I don't know how you can always
look in on a school for poor children.

00:09:15.290 --> 00:09:20.370
And deliberately going out
to where the grimy underclass is?

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:23.040
It's not something we nobles do.

00:09:23.040 --> 00:09:27.700
I bet you caught that cold
you had last week from them.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.700
I hate it.

00:09:38.700 --> 00:09:41.540
I hate this whole world.

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:43.830
And this nation, where the
curse of social standing

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:47.700
places its mark upon the soul by birth...

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:49.500
...I especially hate.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:56.290
Forgive me for not being able
to come by last week.

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.830
I caught a bit of a cold.

00:09:58.830 --> 00:10:01.250
That is quite all right, Lord Moriarty.

00:10:01.250 --> 00:10:05.200
The sentiment alone is enough
to please the children.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:10.330
But frankly, should you not be at home resting?

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:16.330
No, I do not much wish to stay home right now.

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:17.500
Oh?

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:19.700
Hey, come read this book with us!

00:10:19.700 --> 00:10:21.700
Sure, I'll be right there--

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:29.910
Here, it's the new book that
Mr Moriarty gave us earlier!

00:10:29.910 --> 00:10:33.330
I do not believe I have seen those two before.

00:10:33.330 --> 00:10:37.450
Ah, yes, we took those
two brothers in last week.

00:10:37.450 --> 00:10:41.080
The younger one is so frail, the poor thing.

00:10:41.080 --> 00:10:45.330
However, they both know how
to read, and even know Latin.

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:50.580
Moreover, the older one is knowledgeable
enough to leave the adults speechless,

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:54.290
and is interested in maths and chemistry.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:55.750
I understand that before coming here,

00:10:55.750 --> 00:11:00.250
they would go into the reading room
of the British Museum unattended.

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:05.330
Their head librarian asked if we
would take charge of them.

00:11:05.330 --> 00:11:10.040
An orphan... with the knowledge
to leave adults speechless?

00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:15.870
At first, I simply regarded him
as being unusual. That was all.

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:19.120
The thing that triggered my interest in him...

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:21.450
...was really only that.

00:11:29.200 --> 00:11:32.830
You are taking on an orphan as a foster child?

00:11:32.830 --> 00:11:36.290
Yes. Don't you think that is just wonderful?

00:11:36.290 --> 00:11:42.000
Doing so will allow one of those
poor children to be saved by us.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.660
Well, yes, indeed...

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:52.450
Your Grace, I am deeply moved
by your words of abundant charity.

00:11:52.450 --> 00:11:54.000
So then--

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:56.830
I will make arrangements at once

00:11:56.830 --> 00:12:00.250
to welcome an orphan into
my home and raise them.

00:12:00.250 --> 00:12:01.700
Oh, my.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:04.950
I knew you would say as much.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.950
Lord Moriarty,

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:12.080
you will go along with this as well, yes?

00:12:12.080 --> 00:12:14.450
Yes, of course.

00:12:19.410 --> 00:12:20.790
Darling!

00:12:20.790 --> 00:12:23.790
What do you mean, you're taking in an orphan?!

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:27.000
There's nothing more to it.
It's exactly as I said.

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.450
As you said?

00:12:28.450 --> 00:12:33.000
We already have two outstanding
sons in the family! So why?

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:37.830
What's worse, an orphan
from only God knows where!

00:12:37.830 --> 00:12:43.910
Acts of charity are the duty of the nobility.
You know that much, don't you?

00:12:45.160 --> 00:12:47.500
The duchess Pénières, right?

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:52.620
That charity-crazed woman put you
up to this, and that's why...!

00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:56.950
Go take what you said back!
Otherwise, I will go to her myself!

00:12:56.950 --> 00:13:01.330
Don't be absurd! How could I do anything
so disgraceful at this point?!

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:02.910
Darling!

00:13:05.330 --> 00:13:07.620
They sure did bloom beautifully.

00:13:07.620 --> 00:13:13.450
Yes. I did as that boy told me,
and look at them.

00:13:13.450 --> 00:13:15.620
I don't know if he read it in a book,

00:13:15.620 --> 00:13:19.450
but it is astounding that he knows
so much about gardening.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:22.330
Hey, teach us some mathematics today!

00:13:22.330 --> 00:13:25.830
If you can do mathematics,
you can be an accountant, right?

00:13:25.830 --> 00:13:30.000
No! He's going to read us
the next part of the book we got!

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.500
Never mind them! Tell us how to win at chess!

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:38.080
Now, now, children, it won't do
to ask him for everything.

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:39.790
What about you, Teacher?

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:43.250
You had him teach you how to
make cough medicine, didn't you?

00:13:43.250 --> 00:13:45.330
Yes, but that was...

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:08.450
You want <i>me </i>to select which orphan
will be our foster child?

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:11.830
That's right.

00:14:11.830 --> 00:14:15.950
You regularly go to that
ragged school, don't you?

00:14:15.950 --> 00:14:18.620
Go and find us someone suitable.

00:14:18.620 --> 00:14:22.370
Preferably someone well behaved,
who won't give us any trouble.

00:14:24.040 --> 00:14:26.540
Yes, Father.

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:41.120
So when you do the calculation, one person
can advance roughly ten inches per hour.

00:14:41.120 --> 00:14:43.750
The soil in this area is quite firm,

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:48.750
so in order to dig a 40-yard distance,
I would say it will require about a week.

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:51.250
It sounds like you're talking
about something complicated.

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.410
Lord Moriarty...

00:14:55.500 --> 00:15:01.870
Well then... we had best
be getting back to work.

00:15:01.870 --> 00:15:05.120
If we don't get a move on,
we'll never finish today.

00:15:06.830 --> 00:15:08.830
Did I interrupt anything?

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:12.080
No, we finished the important part.

00:15:12.080 --> 00:15:18.450
You're almost like everyone's own
counsellor--or even better, adviser.

00:15:18.450 --> 00:15:21.370
This is how I've always gotten by.

00:15:21.370 --> 00:15:25.540
When I share my knowledge, I'm able
to get food or money in return as thanks.

00:15:25.540 --> 00:15:30.080
It's a much more peaceful life
than turning to thievery.

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:36.200
Besides, if someone is in trouble,
and I can be of help to them,

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.870
I'd like to do whatever I can.

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:47.410
Hey, did you hear?
Old Mr Thompson's safe got broken into.

00:15:47.410 --> 00:15:51.410
Yeah. They got away with all
the valuables he had in his cellar.

00:15:51.410 --> 00:15:56.330
Heh, it was all money he extorted
from the poor. Serves him right.

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:59.370
Still, some bloke must have
a smart head on their shoulders.

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:02.450
They dug a side tunnel from
the sewer to sneak in, right?

00:16:02.450 --> 00:16:07.250
Yeah, but 40 yards is no mean feat.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:17.330
...40 yards is no mean feat.

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:24.620
In order to dig a 40-yard distance,
I would say it will require about a week.

00:16:24.620 --> 00:16:29.200
It can't be. I'm overthinking it.

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:33.580
My word, Lord Moriarty, thank you, as always.

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:37.120
Is something the matter? You look a little pale.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:39.450
Oh, no, nothing.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:42.540
The children are inside the chapel.

00:16:52.250 --> 00:16:55.950
Then, the nobility are great people, right?

00:16:55.950 --> 00:17:03.950
That's right. Every day, they wear fine clothes,
eat delicious food, and sleep in warm beds.

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:08.950
That's because their forefathers
contributed much to the country.

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:11.120
That is why the nobility is great.

00:17:11.120 --> 00:17:12.330
Mm-hmm!

00:17:12.330 --> 00:17:14.910
But there are some caddish nobles, too.

00:17:14.910 --> 00:17:19.080
I've been given dirty looks by people
in carriages, and yelled at by them.

00:17:19.080 --> 00:17:26.000
When my mum worked in the house of a nobleman,
she got put through hell, and ended up dying.

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:30.830
You're right. There are some nobles
who are bad people, too.

00:17:31.870 --> 00:17:35.950
So, everyone, what happens
if a bad nobleman turns up?

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:39.000
Remember? I told you what to do before.

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.830
Fight them!

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:42.620
--Fight them and kill them!
--Fight them and kill them!

00:17:42.620 --> 00:17:47.000
--Fight! Kill! Down with bad nobles!
--Fight! Kill! Down with bad nobles!

00:17:47.000 --> 00:17:52.080
--Fight! Kill! Down with bad nobles...!
--Fight! Kill! Down with bad nobles...!

00:17:55.290 --> 00:18:01.200
If we get rid of the bad people,
this would be an ideal country.

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:04.040
In the eyes of God,

00:18:04.040 --> 00:18:09.040
he has been taking the path of wrong
to achieve a world that is right.

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:20.660
I-I am terribly sorry!

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:28.250
You're back home early, Brother.

00:18:28.250 --> 00:18:30.290
What were you doing?

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:33.910
Just disciplining a servant who was careless.

00:18:33.910 --> 00:18:38.540
Honestly, I'm getting fed up
with low-class people.

00:18:38.540 --> 00:18:41.250
They simply cannot make a proper cup of tea.

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:45.950
I'm going to have to speak
to Father and have her fired.

00:18:58.790 --> 00:19:04.700
You're almost like everyone's own
counsellor--or even better, adviser.

00:19:07.660 --> 00:19:10.950
This is how I've always gotten by.

00:19:10.950 --> 00:19:15.450
When I share my knowledge, I'm able
to get food or money in return as thanks.

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:24.290
Honestly, I'm getting fed up
with low-class people.

00:19:25.750 --> 00:19:26.620
Fight them!

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:28.200
--Fight them and kill them!
--Fight them and kill them!

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:30.870
--Down with bad nobles!
--Down with bad nobles!

00:19:31.830 --> 00:19:36.750
If someone is in trouble,
and I can be of help to them,

00:19:36.750 --> 00:19:39.330
I'd like to do whatever I can.

00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:54.540
What did you want to speak about?

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:59.620
"Down with bad nobles."

00:19:59.620 --> 00:20:02.540
You heard that, did you?

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:04.870
It was an outstanding lecture.

00:20:04.870 --> 00:20:11.370
However, turning the nobility against you
means picking a quarrel with the whole country.

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:13.080
Can you fight them?

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:14.620
The whole country?

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:23.500
That is what I mean to do.

00:20:25.000 --> 00:20:28.410
Our lives should have the same value...

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:33.910
Everyone should have an
equal right to happiness...

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:36.330
But in this country, that doesn't exist.

00:20:37.450 --> 00:20:40.830
This class system places a curse upon people.

00:20:40.830 --> 00:20:46.700
Because of it, people's hearts are tainted
and twisted, giving rise to devils.

00:20:46.700 --> 00:20:50.580
In which case, the opposite is also true.

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:53.870
Once the devils are cast out,
people's hearts become clear again,

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.160
and the curse is lifted.

00:20:56.160 --> 00:21:00.000
The country will assuredly be beautiful.

00:21:01.830 --> 00:21:05.580
Will you report me to Scotland Yard?

00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:12.700
You are a nobleman; wouldn't you
like to see something like that?

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:17.080
<i>An oath committed by souls assumed,</i>

00:21:17.080 --> 00:21:21.330
<i>with ideals that wallow in genetic karma</i>

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:40.410
<i>Lie! Be resolute if you're going</i>
<i>to share your pain</i>

00:21:40.410 --> 00:21:42.660
<i>(Demonstrate your resolve)</i>

00:21:42.660 --> 00:21:46.160
<i>Like, dislike, you can't afford</i>
<i>to care either way</i>

00:21:46.160 --> 00:21:49.370
<i>It depends on the objective</i>
<i>(Making it happen is what's most important)</i>

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:52.870
<i>The necessary evil of self-sacrifice</i>

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:56.500
<i>is a righteous cause that no one can comprehend</i>

00:21:56.500 --> 00:22:00.250
<i>Take pride in the inviolable bonds shared</i>

00:22:00.250 --> 00:22:05.120
<i>among brothers who bear the same crime</i>

00:22:05.120 --> 00:22:08.790
<i>Make a chance trigger your inevitable stance</i>

00:22:08.790 --> 00:22:10.450
<i>and get drunk on your accomplishments</i>

00:22:10.450 --> 00:22:12.250
<i>at the end</i>

00:22:12.250 --> 00:22:15.410
<i>Don't believe in what you can see,</i>

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:19.660
<i>in truths there's no point in knowing</i>
<i>(Whatever it takes)</i>

00:22:19.660 --> 00:22:26.250
<i>Defer to its own validity,</i>
<i>you only have one goal</i>

00:22:26.250 --> 00:22:27.750
<i>(Let me hear you say)</i>

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:34.620
<i>You can't lie to yourself, come along with me</i>

00:22:37.500 --> 00:22:40.200
<i>It's all because there is no answer</i>

00:22:40.200 --> 00:22:42.580
<i>There is no turning back</i>

00:22:54.540 --> 00:22:59.250
An orphan... with the knowledge
to leave adults speechless?

00:22:59.250 --> 00:23:05.120
At first, I simply regarded him
as being unusual. That was all.

00:23:05.120 --> 00:23:08.160
The thing that triggered my interest in him...

00:23:08.160 --> 00:23:11.620
...was really only that.

00:23:30.620 --> 00:23:32.950
A-Are you all right?!

00:23:32.950 --> 00:23:35.870
Doctor! Quickly!

00:23:35.870 --> 00:23:37.540
Who are you?

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:39.620
Albert.

00:23:39.620 --> 00:23:42.410
Albert James Moriarty.

00:23:43.620 --> 00:23:45.200
And these...

00:23:46.450 --> 00:23:51.870
Next time on <i>Moriarty the Patriot</i>:
"The Scarlet Eyes Act 2"
